The four element in a counter controlled iteration are mentioned below and note this is relating mainly to for loop fo example 

for(int count = 1; count <= 10; count++){
    System.out.print(count);
}



So the count is the control variable it helps us track how many times the loop is executed


Initialization this is were the loop will be starting from 


Increment or Decrement This help us to change the variable after every loop which is count ++ or can be ++countOne



The Condition which determines or tells us when the loop should stop 
